    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`make_nvfp4_moe_quant_config` recreates `a1_gscale = 1 / a13_scale` (read by `prepare()` for input quantization) on every `process_weights_after_loading`. Because it is not a parameter, weight reload never restores it into the storage captured by CUDA graphs. After `sleep(level=2)` that storage is gone and MoE outputs become garbage. This PR keeps the reciprocal scales as layer parameters, like `g1_scale_c`. It covers the \"NVFP4 reciprocal-scale chains\" item of #48312.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `sleep(level=2)` + `wake_up` + `reload_weights` no longer corrupts NVFP4 MoE outputs under CUDA graphs.\n- No change for plain reloads, or when no layer is passed.\n\n## Validation\n\nGB300, RedHatAI/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 (FlashInfer TRT-LLM MoE), TP1, CUDA graphs. 8 greedy prompts compared with the cold run:\n\n| | `reload_weights` | `sleep(2)` + `wake_up` + `reload_weights` |\n|---|---|---|\n| main | 8/8 | 0/8 |\n| this PR | 8/8 | 8/8 |\n\nGSM8K (1319, 5-shot): main 59.89% cold → 16.83% after `sleep(2)` + reload; this PR 59.89% → 59.89%.\n\n```python\nllm = LLM(\"RedHatAI/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4\", enable_sleep_mode=True)\ncold = llm.generate(prompts, greedy)\nllm.sleep(level=2); llm.wake_up(); llm.collective_rpc(\"reload_weights\")\nafter = llm.generate(prompts, greedy)   # main: every prompt differs\n```\n\n```bash\npytest tests/kernels/moe/test_nvfp4_moe_quant_config_reload.py   # 1 passed (new)\npytest tests/kernels/moe/test_trtllm_nvfp4_moe.py                # 23 passed on main and this PR\n```\n\n## Details\n\n- With a layer, the two reciprocals are kept via `replace_parameter(layer, \"moe_a1_gscale\"/\"moe_a2_gscale\", ..., prefer_copy=True)`. Layerwise reload restores parameters into their capture-time storage. New names avoid clashing with compressed-tensors' `w13_input_global_scale` checkpoint parameter.\n- #49789 (`ReloadArena`) also stabilizes these tensors, but only for the CUTLASS backends. This 9-line fix also covers TRT-LLM.\n- Not tested with EPLB.\n- No other open PR addresses this (searched \"nvfp4 a1_gscale reload\", \"48312 in:body nvfp4\").\n- AI assistance (Claude Code) was used; I reviewed every changed line and the results.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
